      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`OCP_MXQuantizationEmulationTritonExperts.apply()` hardcoded `a2_scale=None` in its `super().apply(...)` call, so the checkpoint's static second-GEMM activation scale never reached the quantizer. The emulated MoE silently fake-quantized the second GEMM against a **dynamic per-tensor amax** instead of the static scale the checkpoint declares.\r\n\r\n### Affected scheme/model\r\n\r\n- Exactly one scheme: **Quark `w_mxfp4_a_fp8` on the `EMULATION` backend.**\r\n- Example model: https://huggingface.co/amd/gpt-oss-120b-w-mxfp4-a-fp8\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n### New regression test\r\n\r\n`test_ocp_mx_emulation_forwards_a2_scale` is added to `tests/kernels/moe/test_ocp_mx_moe.py`\r\n\r\n### End-to-end test\r\n- `amd/gpt-oss-120b-w-mxfp4-a-fp8`\r\n- on MI325X (gfx942), ROCm, torch 2.10.0.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# On gfx942 emulation is the auto-selected backend; --moe-backend emulation pins it.\r\nvllm serve amd/gpt-oss-120b-w-mxfp4-a-fp8 \\\r\n  --moe-backend emulation --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\r\n  --reasoning-parser openai_gptoss --trust-remote-code\r\n\r\nlm_eval --model local-chat-completions \\\r\n  --model_args base_url=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions,num_concurrent=64 \\\r\n  --tasks gsm8k_platinum --num_fewshot 5 \\\r\n  --gen_kwargs max_gen_toks=2048 --apply_chat_template --fewshot_as_multiturn\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n### **_The regression test_**\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python -m pytest tests/kernels/moe/test_ocp_mx_moe.py -q -k \"a2_scale or emulation_rounds\"\r\n5 passed, 133 deselected, 15 warnings in 5.48s\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf reverting to current upstream/main, then failed:\r\n\r\n```\r\n>       assert captured[\"a2_scale\"] is a2_scale\r\nE       assert None is tensor([0.1250])\r\n1 failed, 137 deselected, 15 warnings in 3.79s\r\n```\r\n\r\n### The end-to-end test\r\n\r\nFor the end-to-end serving, there is no crash to show, nothing raises, nothing warns, and the model serves and scores normally (a quiet bug from end-to-end view).\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
